# Google Services — Firebase was removed (decision log D1) and this app has no
# INTERNET permission, so no google-services.json should ever exist here. Kept
# ignored so an accidental re-add can't be committed.
google-services.json

# Freeline
freeline.py
freeline/
freeline_project_description.json

# fastlane
fastlane/report.xml
fastlane/Preview.html
fastlane/screenshots
fastlane/test_output
fastlane/readme.md

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets and credentials
#
# Verified as of this commit: nothing matching these patterns is tracked, and
# `git log --all --diff-filter=A` shows none was ever committed and later
# removed. These patterns exist so that stays true.
#
# Note the signing keystore is never a file in this tree: it is materialised at
# build time from $ANDROID_KEYSTORE_BASE64 into app/build/keystore.jks, which
# `build/` above already ignores. Passwords come from environment variables
# only (see app/build.gradle.kts) — never a properties file.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.p12
*.pfx
*.pem
*.key
*.der
secrets.properties
keystore.properties
signing.properties
service-account*.json

# MCP server configs. `claude mcp add --scope project` writes .mcp.json into
# the repo root, and auth headers (API keys, tokens) go in it verbatim. Ignored
# so a credential cannot be committed by an editor's "stage all".
.mcp.json
.mcp.local.json

# Node / JS tooling. This is a pure Kotlin/Gradle project with no JS build, so
# these should never appear — ignored defensively rather than because they do.
node_modules/
.expo/
npm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*

# Large model weights. The one model this app ships (assets/mobile_face_net.tflite,
# ~5 MB, checksum-pinned) is deliberately committed, so *.tflite is NOT ignored.
# .gguf is listed because the roadmap contemplates an on-device LLM caption
# feature, and multi-gigabyte weights must never be committed by reflex.
*.gguf
*.onnx
*.safetensors
